@@ -3,3 +3,16 @@
 A small TypeScript library, with no runtime dependency, of building blocks for our services that store,
 exchange and update JSON: configuration files, API payloads and stored records. It is imported by the
 other projects of the team, so its behaviour must follow the published standards it implements.
+
+## JSON Pointer (RFC 6901)
+
+`resolvePointer(document, pointer)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, returns the value of a JSON document
+that a JSON Pointer refers to. It throws a `SyntaxError` (or a `TypeError` for a non-string pointer) when
+the pointer is invalid, and a `RangeError` when it does not resolve to a value of the document.
+
+```ts
+resolvePointer({ "a/b": [10, 20] }, "/a~1b/1"); // 20
+```
+
+Strictness follows the RFC: array tokens must be canonical indexes (no leading zeros), the token `-`
+never resolves, and only own members of objects are followed.
